# ==== T-FMT-D (R41) fill-pack matrix — LIST KIND = CALL-ARGUMENT list.
#
# SUBJECT: this fixture asserts `gg fmt` OUTPUT (byte-for-byte, in
# `fmt_fill_pack_call_args_kind`) — a bulk `gg fmt` sweep MUST EXCLUDE it.
#
# Emit site: `Formatter::format_call_args_wrapped` -> `doc::surround_fill("(", .., ")")`.
#
# Axis cell claim (Core #12 — `list kind x fit` for the CALL-ARG kind ONLY):
#   c_empty  empty              `()` — the commonest list shape in any program
#   c_flat   fits-flat          one line, no trailing comma
#   c_fill   needs-fill         greedy packing at the block continuation indent.
#                               This is the owner's `draw_text_atlas` shape; its
#                               break points are DERIVED at MAX_WIDTH = 120, not
#                               copied from the width-100 rendering in the ask.
#   c_over   single-over-width  the one argument does not fit on the open-delimiter
#                               line, so it breaks to the continuation indent, alone
#
# RED source per row: c_fill / c_over are TRUE pre-fix REDs (one argument per
# line with a trailing comma). c_empty / c_flat are invariant — break-and-restore
# them by lowering `doc::MAX_WIDTH`.
void c_empty():
    draw_text_atlas()

void c_flat():
    draw_text_atlas(ctxValue, fontValue, textValue)

void c_fill():
    draw_text_atlas(ctxValue, fontValue, textValue, xxValue, yyValue, charSizeValue, rrValue, ggValue, bbValue, aaValue)

void c_over():
    draw_text_atlas(aSingleCallArgumentIdentifierWhoseRenderedWidthAloneExceedsTheEntireLineBudgetOfTheFormatterAndThenSome)
